SUMMARY
-------
Native SwiftUI implementation of the API Playground page at page-level parity:
two glass panels (sidebar + main), the four catalogue data states, and the four
i18n strings, adaptive across macOS (regular) and iOS (compact/regular). All
state is driven by an @Observable `ApiPlaygroundPageModel` through an injectable
`ApiPlaygroundCatalog` seam (production wires the shared KMP OpenAPI source,
ADR-004; previews/tests inject a static catalogue). The page is self-contained
so it does not depend on the two colliding feature-view types (see BLOCKERS).

Navigation registration: `ApiPlaygroundRouteRegistration.register(into:)` folds
the page into the shared `AppRouteHostRegistry` (rendered by the AppShell
NavigationSplitView/TabView) under the `.admin` route; `TeslaSyncApp` composes it
into the environment registry; `AppRouteParser` maps the `/api-playground` deep
link to `.admin` (alongside the existing `/devtools` alias family).

FILES ADDED (apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Admin/)
  ApiPlaygroundPage.swift              View: header + adaptive 2-pane + panels
  ApiPlaygroundPageViews.swift         Sidebar (4 states) + detail subviews
  ApiPlaygroundPageModel.swift         DataState, endpoint type, seam, model, query
  ApiPlaygroundReference.swift         Real TeslaSync REST surface (router.go mirror)
  ApiPlaygroundRouteRegistration.swift Route registry registration (.admin)
FILES TOUCHED (navigation/build registration — allowed)
  Sources/TeslaSyncApp.swift           compose ApiPlayground registration
  Sources/App/AppRouteParser.swift     /api-playground -> .admin deep-link alias
  project.yml                          + TeslaSync/Features source path (iOS + macOS)
  .swiftlint.yml                       + TeslaSync/Features to included
Strings: all 4 parity keys already present in Localization/Localizable.xcstrings
  under the catalog `translation.playground.*` namespace (BatteryCells widget
  precedent). No catalog mutation required.

