    BLOCKER A (build-blocking DEFECT, cross-runner):
      `public enum HTTPMethod` and `public struct ParsedEndpoint` are each
      redeclared in TWO files in the same target module:
        TeslaSync/feature-views/EndpointSidebar.Models.swift
        TeslaSync/feature-views/RequestBuilder.Adapter.swift
      Reproduction (real SDK, this host):
        swiftc -typecheck EndpointSidebar.Models.swift RequestBuilder.Adapter.swift
        -> error: invalid redeclaration of 'HTTPMethod'
        -> error: 'HTTPMethod' is ambiguous for type lookup in this context
      This is a parallel-merge collision between the P3 EndpointSidebar (0029)
      and RequestBuilder (0040) component prompts. It fails the TeslaSync target
      compile on ANY runner (incl. macos-latest) until those component owners
      de-duplicate the type. It is NOT in this prompt's allowed file set
      (apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Admin/**, nav registration, the string
      catalog, this log). The page was therefore implemented self-contained and
      does NOT depend on either colliding type.

    BLOCKER B (host capability, macOS-pending):
      Frameworks/Shared.xcframework is not staged (only .gitkeep). It is produced
      by a Kotlin/Native Gradle build (scheme pre-action). 15 app files
      `import Shared`, so the full target cannot compile without it. On this host
      the build is also contended by many parallel slots assembling the same
      XCFramework. This mirrors the existing macos-pending row for
      p1-shared/S3-0001 (Shared.xcframework binary deferred to macOS CI).

